# SECRETS - never commit
# Case variants matter: gitignore is case-sensitive on Linux and macOS.
# Match anywhere in the name, not only at the start. A file called
# ai_automation_api_keys.txt is a real filename on this machine and an earlier
# version of these rules did NOT catch it, because the pattern was anchored to
# the front. Verified: it is caught now.
*api_key*
*api_keys*
*API_KEY*
*API_Keys*
*apikey*
*APIKEY*
*api-key*
*_keys.txt
*_KEYS.txt
*.key
*.pem
*.pfx
*.p12
*.token
.env
.env.*
*.env
.envrc
credentials.json
secrets/
_secrets/

# Demo and classroom artifacts.
# The Unit 0 Thursday .gitignore demonstration creates a file named secrets.txt
# containing a fake key. "secrets/" above matches a directory, not that file.
# Without the line below, running the demo anywhere in this tree tracks it.
secrets.txt
scratch.txt

# STUDENT DATA - never commit, in either repository
# This is a school. Anything with a real student's name, grade, schedule, or work
# in it does not belong in version control, private repository or not.
grades/
rosters/
student-work/
submissions/
*roster*.csv
*roster*.xlsx
*grades*.csv
*grades*.xlsx
*.gradebook

# Build artifacts
node_modules/
*.pdf.tmp
~$*
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Generated slide decks ARE committed to the instructor repository.
# They are the artifact projected in class, and having them on any machine you
# clone to is worth more than the few megabytes. The .md outline remains the
# source of truth; the export is a convenience.
# To stop tracking them, uncomment the next line.
# **/exports/

# Gamma sidecars record which generation produced which deck. Keep them.
# *.gamma.json  <- deliberately NOT ignored
